# DURABLE REPRO — D10 exclusivity hole A9: the nested-writer conflict inside an
# INDEX-STORE (`dst[0] = pick(v[0], mutate(&v))`).
#
# Sibling of `sound_excl_nested_writer_call.gg`. An index store lowers to a
# `__set`/`__put`-shaped call whose value operand is a whole expression tree; if
# that tree is not walked for participants, every conflict inside it escapes.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg, C backend, `--sanitize`): `gg check`
# clean, then AddressSanitizer heap-use-after-free in
# `gorget_string_clone_to_owned` (reported inside `pick`).
#
# INTENDED: REJECTED at `gg check` with `E_BorrowConflict`.
#
# The 4096-push loop FORCES a real reallocation; `dst` is a separate collection
# so the only overlap in the program is the intended one.
#
#
# ORACLE (ggdef, measured this session): ACCEPTS this program and prints the
# pre-mutation value. ggdef is a definitional INTERPRETER with value semantics,
# so a reallocation cannot invalidate anything and this UAF class is
# structurally unobservable in that lane — it is NOT the authority here. The
# intended REJECT comes from the ratified D10 exclusivity ruling, which ggdef
# owes as part of the same landing (Core #9). Full note in
# `sound_excl_getchain_local.gg`.
# Cited from TODO.md (CoW / ownership / High): the D10 "one exclusive writer"
# structural-chokepoint entry (nested-writer costume, index-store sibling).
int mutate(Vector[String] &v):
    int i = 0
    while i < 4096:
        v.push("filler-padding-to-force-a-real-reallocation")
        i = i + 1
    return v.len()

String pick(String s, int n):
    return s

void main():
    Vector[String] v = Vector[String]()
    v.push("alpha-heap-forced-payload")
    Vector[String] dst = Vector[String]()
    dst.push("placeholder-destination-payload")
    dst[0] = pick(v[0], mutate(&v))
    print(dst[0])
